{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: pdf","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_rag_abdelnabi2025llmailinject"],"evidence_ids":["ev_rag_injection_defenses_0005","ev_rag_injection_defenses_0026"],"id":"claim_rag_llmail_dataset_scale","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"208,095 unique attack submissions from 839 participants","topic":"rag_injection_defenses"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_rag_liu2023lostinmiddle"],"evidence_ids":["ev_rag_injection_defenses_0035"],"id":"claim_rag_lostinmiddle_chunk_rank_salience","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"Injection-relevant reading: because attention is U-shaped over context position, a retrieved chunk's rank in the assembled prompt changes how strongly it is attended \u2014 an injected/poisoned chunk surfaced at the head or tail of the context is more salient (more likely to drive output) than the same chunk buried in the middle. Retrieval-side defenses that re-rank or reposition retrieved spans therefore alter injection efficacy independent of the chunk's content.","topic":"rag_injection_defenses"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_rag_liu2023lostinmiddle"],"evidence_ids":["ev_rag_injection_defenses_0034"],"id":"claim_rag_lostinmiddle_position_sensitivity","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"performance can degrade significantly when changing the position of relevant information","topic":"rag_injection_defenses"}
{"claim_type":"fact","confidence":{"factors":["source: primary","verified: webfetch"],"score":0.95},"entity_ids":["ent_rag_liu2023lostinmiddle"],"evidence_ids":["ev_rag_injection_defenses_0033"],"id":"claim_rag_lostinmiddle_positional_attention","record_type":"claim","status":"active","text":"performance is often highest when relevant information occurs at the beginning or end of the input context, and significantly degrades when models must access relevant information in the middle of long contexts","topic":"rag_injection_defenses"}
